{"mock":{"w":"mock","zh":[],"ipa":{"uk":"/mɒk/","us":"/mɑk/"},"ety":[{"n":1,"chain":[{"l":"enm","f":"mokken","t":"inh"},{"l":"fro","f":"mocquer","t":"der"},{"l":"dum","f":"mocken","t":"der","g":"to mumble"},{"l":"gml","f":"mucken","t":"der","g":"to grumble, talk with the mouth half-opened"},{"l":"gmw-pro","f":"*mokkijan","t":"der"},{"l":"gem-pro","f":"*mukkijaną","t":"der"},{"l":"ine-pro","f":"*mūg-","t":"der"}],"text":"From Middle English mokken, from Old French mocquer, moquier (“to deride, jeer”), from Middle Dutch mocken (“to mumble”) or Middle Low German mucken (“to grumble, talk with the mouth half-opened”), both from Proto-West Germanic *mokkijan, *mukkijan (“to low, bellow; mumble”), from Proto-Germanic *mukkijaną, *mūhaną (“to low, bellow, shout”), from Proto-Indo-European *mūg-, *mūk- (“to low, mumble”).","cog":[{"l":"nl","f":"mokken"},{"l":"goh","f":"firmucken"},{"l":"de","f":"mucksen"},{"l":"fy","f":"mokke"},{"l":"sv","f":"mucka"},{"l":"nl","f":"mokkel"}]}],"pos":[{"p":"noun","e":0,"senses":[{"d":"An imitation, usually of lesser quality.","ex":["Is tortured thirst itself too sweet a cup?\nGall, and more bitter mocks, shall make it up."],"grp":0},{"d":"Mockery; the act of mocking.","ex":["Fooles make a mocke at ſinne: but among the righteous there is fauour."],"grp":2},{"d":"A mockup or prototype; particularly, ellipsis of mock object, as used in unit testing.","tags":["computing","mathematics"],"ex":["Mocks replace the objects with which your methods under test collaborate, thus offering a layer of isolation."]}],"forms":[["pl","mocks"]]},{"p":"verb","e":0,"senses":[{"d":"To mimic, to simulate.","ex":["To see the life as lively mocked as ever / Still sleep mocked death.","Mocking marriage with a dame of France."],"grp":3},{"d":"To create an artistic representation of.","tags":["rare"]},{"d":"To make fun of, especially by mimicking; to taunt.","ex":["Let not ambition mock their useful toil."],"grp":4},{"d":"To tantalise, and disappoint the hopes of.","ex"